  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1050 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nNot much to talk about in the longer term portion of the forecast,\nwith the system bringing the showers to the area today and\ntonight to gradually shear out across West Texas. This keeps a\ngood chance of showers across the area for Sunday and Sunday\nnight, before tapering off on Monday. As mentioned yesterday,\nthere will likely be a fairly sharp cutoff to the rain chances and\nrain totals from south to north across the area, with the best\nchances and highest totals likely south of a San Angelo to Brady\nline for Sunday into Monday as the main area of lift shifts into\nthe Rio Grande River Valley and then into Central Texas. In fact \nrain chances are slim for the northern portions of the area after\nSaturday night.\n\nIn any case, looks like a predominantly dry next week, as the \nupper level high that is centered across the Southwest US ridges \ninto Texas. Large upper level trough over the eastern portions of \nthe country will produce a drier northwest flow across the \nSouthern Plains. Temperatures should be pretty close to seasonal \nnorms with lows in the 50s and highs in the 70s.",
